                "In the pre-dawn chill of the Forgotten Observatory, Lyra&#039;s breath plumes as Kael methodically wipes the dew-slicked tiles where her boots had rested—his synthetic fingers, sheathed in nano-weave, erase her thermal signature with clinical precision. &#039;They&#039;ll scan for organic residue by sunrise,&#039; he murmurs, though his hand lingers fractionally where her heel had been, the air between them thick with unspoken itineraries. A single garnet-hued moss frond, crushed under the edge of his utility belt, releases a poignant, earthy scent as he shifts, the observatory&#039;s dormant machinery humming a low counterpoint to their shared silence."
